Part 1 — ClassExp to ProcExp Transformation

(define pi 3.14) 
(define square (lambda (x) (* x x))) 
(define circle (lambda (x y radius) 
    (lambda (msg) 
        (if (eq? msg 'area) 
            (* (square radius) pi) 
            (if (eq? msg 'perimeter)   
                (* 2 pi radius) 
                'error))))) 

(define c (circle 0 0 3)) 
(c 'area)


Part 2 — L3applicativeEval Trace (Substitution Model) Expressions in the order they are evaluated:

1. 3.14 — value expression of (define pi 3.14)

2. (lambda (x) (* x x)) — value expression of (define square ...)

3. (lambda (x y radius)
     (lambda (msg)
       (if (eq? msg 'area)
           (* (square radius) pi)
           (if (eq? msg 'perimeter)
               (* 2 pi radius)
               'error)))) — value expression of (define circle ...)

4. (circle 0 0 3) — value expression of (define c ...)

5. circle — evaluating the rator

6. 0 — first rand

7. 0 — second rand

8. 3 — third rand

9. (lambda (msg)
     (if (eq? msg 'area)
         (* (square 3) pi)
         (if (eq? msg 'perimeter)
             (* 2 pi 3)
             'error))) — body of circle after substitution: x → 0, y → 0, radius → 3

10. (c 'area) — final expression of the program

11. c — evaluating the rator

12. 'area — evaluating the rand

13. (if (eq? 'area 'area)
        (* (square 3) pi)
        (if (eq? 'area 'perimeter)
            (* 2 pi 3)
            'error)) — body of c after substitution: msg → 'area

14. (eq? 'area 'area) — the if condition

15. eq? — rator of the condition

16. 'area — first rand of the condition

17. 'area — second rand of the condition, result: #t

18. (* (square 3) pi) — the then branch

19. * — rator of multiplication

20. (square 3) — first rand

21. square — rator of (square 3)

22. 3 — rand of (square 3)

23. (* 3 3) — body of square after substitution: x → 3

24. * — rator of multiplication

25. 3 — first rand

26. 3 — second rand, result: 9

27. pi — second rand of (* (square 3) pi), returns 3.14

final result:
(* 9 3.14) = 28.26